  "question": "Given $$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},$$ find a matrix $B$ of the same order such that $A+B=O$, where $O$ is the zero matrix of order $2$. Verify your answer.",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "<b>Additive condition</b><br>From $A+B=O$, we obtain $B=-A$.<br><b>Required matrix</b><br>$$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$$<br><b>Verification</b><br>$$A+B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}=O$$",
